> This is quite informative. This is definitely a thread to keep. I was
> wondering if anyone has any information about the AlphaServer 4100. 
> What
> sort of RAM does it use?

   The AS4100 uses AS4100 RAM boards...not SIMMs or DIMMs of any kind.  
They're installed in pairs.  Due to their relatively young age, these 
boards are very easy to find from vendors in various capacities, but 
they typically cost thousands of dollars.  If you're shopping for an 
AS4100 (and I wholeheartedly recommend them if you want a high-end 
machine) it's best to find one with RAM.

